"gloss":"rule"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"உம்","gloss":"relative participle suffix"}],"gloss":"ruling"},{"surface":"வேந்தர்க்கு","parts":[{"text":"வேந்தர்","lemma":"வேந்தர்","gloss":"kings"},{"text":"கு","lemma":"கு","gloss":"dative case suffix"}],"gloss":"to the kings"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"கண்படை","parts":[{"text":"கண்","lemma":"கண்","gloss":"eye"},{"text":"படை","lemma":"படை","gloss":"bed/sleep"}],"gloss":"sleep"},{"surface":"ஈயா","parts":[{"text":"ஈ","lemma":"ஈ","gloss":"give"},{"text":"யா","lemma":"யா","gloss":"not"}],"gloss":"not giving"},{"surface":"வேலோன்","parts":[{"text":"வேல்","lemma":"வேல்","gloss":"spear"},{"text":"ஓன்","lemma":"ஓன்","gloss":"he who has"}],"gloss":"spear-man"},{"surface":"ஊரே","parts":[{"text":"ஊர்","lemma":"ஊர்","gloss":"village"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"is the village indeed"}]}],"literal":"Ploughed-village bull's old horn like / forked-thorn spurge's rough trunk fitting / new millet harvested-stubble bandicoot-rat watching / sparse-haired children bow taking if they shout / big-eyed small hare black pots breaking / in the common ground leaps, of the dry land it is! / Sugarcane's press if it roars, nearby / dark-backed vāḷai fish leaps in that place / cool agricultural tract ruling kings to / sleep not giving spear-man's village indeed!","translation":"The village is in the dry forest land, where big-eyed small hares, watching for bandicoot rats in the stubble of newly harvested millet near the rough trunks of forked-thorn spurge cactus (which look like the curved horns of old village plough-bulls), leap into the common ground, breaking the black cooking pots when sparse-haired children raise their bows and shout. This dry land lies right next to the fertile fields where, when the sugarcane presses roar, dark-backed vāḷai fish leap in the nearby waters. This is the village of the warrior with the spear, who does not allow the kings ruling the cool, fertile agricultural tracts to sleep in peace!","modern":"உழுது பழகிய எருதின் வளைந்த கொம்பைப் போன்ற கவடுள்ள முட்களைக் கொண்ட கள்ளியின் சொரசொரப்பான அடிமரத்தில் ஒண்டிக்கொண்டு, புதிய வரகு அறுவடை செய்த தாள்களில் உள்ள பெருச்சாளிகளைப் பார்த்துக் கொண்டிருக்கும் பெரிய கண்களைக் கொண்ட சிறிய முயல்கள், மெல்லிய தலையையுடைய சிறுவர்கள் வில்லைக் கையில் எடுத்து ஆரவாரம் செய்யும்போது அஞ்சி ஓடி, மன்றத்தில் உள்ள சமையல் கரிய பானைகளை உடைக்கும்படி பாய்கின்ற வன்புலத்தைச் சார்ந்தது அவ்வூர். கரும்பு பிழியும் எந்திரத்தின் சத்தம் கேட்டால், அதற்கு அருகிலுள்ள நீர்நிலைகளில் கரிய முதுகைக் கொண்ட வாளை மீன்கள் துள்ளிப் பாயும் வளமான மருத நிலத்தின் எல்லையில் அது உள்ளது. குளிர்ந்த வயல்நிலங்களை ஆளும் வேந்தர்களுக்குத் தூக்கத்தைக் கொடுக்காத வேலேந்திய வீரனின் ஊர் இதுவேயாகும்.","explanation":"This poem belongs to the Vākai tiṇai and Vallāṇ Mullai tuṟai, which praises the valor of a warrior and describes his territory. The poet Āvūr Kiḻār describes the warrior's village, which is situated on the border between the dry forest land (mullai/pālai) and the fertile agricultural land (marutam). In the dry land, children chasing bandicoot rats scare the hares, which leap and break the black pots in the common ground. Right next to this dry tract is the fertile land where sugarcane presses roar and fish leap. The poet concludes that this small, rugged village belongs to a fierce spear-warrior who keeps the mighty kings of the fertile plains awake at night with fear.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.15,0.6],[0.6,0.83],[0.94,1.4],[1.4,1.52],[1.75,2.1],[2.1,2.79],[2.79,3.2],[3.2,3.6],[3.6,4.21],[4.21,4.7],[4.7,5.5],[5.5,5.7],[5.7,6.53],[6.53,7.2],[7.2,7.7],[7.7,8.1],[8.1,9.4],[9.4,9.9],[9.9,10.5],[10.5,10.8],[10.8,11.5],[11.5,11.9],[11.9,12.62],[12.71,13.08],[13.08,13.7],[13.7,13.9],[13.9,14.7],[14.7,15.0],[15.0,16.0],[16.0,16.3],[16.3,16.7],[16.7,17.0],[18.04,18.64],[18.64,19.04],[19.04,19.24],[19.24,20.14],[20.14,20.44],[20.44,20.68],[20.68,20.84]],"female":[[0.17,0.7],[0.7,0.94],[1.19,1.8],[1.8,2.23],[2.23,2.8],[2.8,3.2],[3.33,3.6],[3.6,4.5],[4.5,5.3],[5.5,5.7],[5.7,6.4],[6.4,6.58],[6.58,7.35],[7.35,7.97],[7.97,8.9],[8.9,9.1],[9.1,10.15],[10.95,11.21],[11.21,11.74],[11.74,12.0],[12.0,12.8],[12.8,13.2],[13.2,13.76],[13.82,14.3],[14.3,15.1],[15.1,15.3],[15.3,16.1],[16.1,16.5],[16.5,17.6],[17.6,17.9],[17.9,18.3],[18.3,18.7],[19.84,20.64],[20.7,20.94],[20.94,21.54],[21.54,22.54],[22.54,22.78],[22.78,23.14],[23.14,23.64]]},"sync":[[["உழுது","having ploughed"],["ஊர்","roaming"]],[["காளை","bull"]],[["ஊழ்","old"],["கோடு","horn"]],[["அன்ன","like"]],[["கவை","forked"],["முள்","thorn"]],[["கள்ளி","spurge cactus"],["பொரி","rough"]],[["பொரி","rough"],["அரை","trunk"]],[["பொருந்தி","staying close to"]],[["புது","new"],["வரகு","millet"]],[["அரிகால்","harvested stubble"]],[["கருப்பை","bandicoot rat"]],[["பார்க்கும்","watching"]],[["புன்","sparse"],["தலை","haired"]],[["சிறாஅர்","children"]],[["வில்","bow"],["எடுத்து","taking"]],[["ஆர்ப்பின்","if they shout"]],[["பெருங்கண்","big-eyed"]],[["குறுமுயல்","small hare"]],[["கருங்கலன்","black pots"]],[["உடைய","breaking"]],[["மன்றிற்","in the common ground"]],[["பாயும்","leaping"]],[["வன்புலத்ததுவே","is of the dry land indeed"]],[["வன்புலத்ததுவே","is of the dry land indeed"]],[["கரும்பின்","of sugarcane"]],[["எந்திரம்","press"]],[["சிலைப்பின்","if it roars"]],[["அயலது","that which is nearby"]],[["இருஞ்சுவல்","dark-backed"]],[["வாளை","scabbard fish"]],[["பிறழும்","leaping"]],[["ஆங்கண்","in that place"]],[["தண்பணை","cool agricultural tract"]],[["ஆளும்","ruling"]],[["வேந்தர்க்கு","to the kings"]],[["கண்படை","sleep"]],[["ஈயா","not giving"]],[["வேலோன்","spear-man"]],[["ஊரே","is the village indeed"]]]}